    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "High blood pressure (hypertension) is usually called the \"silent killer\" because it typically causes no obvious signs or symptoms at all, even when it reaches dangerous levels.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "\"silent killer\"",
            "link": "https://www.heart.org/en/health-topics/high-blood-pressure/know-your-risk-factors-for-high-blood-pressure/what-are-the-symptoms-of-high-blood-pressure"
          }
        ],
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "no obvious signs or symptoms at all"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "The Asymptomatic Reality"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "No clues: You can have high blood pressure for years without feeling any different."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Testing is key: The only way to know your numbers is to have your blood pressure checked with a cuff."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Normal vs. High: A normal reading is below 120/80 mm Hg, while high blood pressure is consistently at or above 130/80 mm Hg."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Signs of a Dangerous Spike (Hypertensive Crisis)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "When blood pressure spikes extremely high (above 180/120 mm Hg), rare or severe symptoms can appear. Seek immediate medical care if a very high reading is accompanied by:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Severe, sudden headache"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Chest pain or tightness"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Shortness of breath"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Sudden vision changes or blurry vision"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Confusion, dizziness, or fatigue"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Signs of a stroke (facial drooping, slurred speech, or weakness)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Your recent blood pressure readings (if you have them)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Whether you are experiencing any specific symptoms right now"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you understand what those numbers mean or when to seek professional care."
      }
    ],
